10	 * Step of {@code POST /api/owners}, the duplicate block, that rejects a create whose derived identity
11	 * (see {@link OwnerIdentity}) collides with an existing owner's, throwing
12	 * {@link DuplicateIdentityException} (handled as 409 Conflict).
13	 *
14	 * <p>Two owners are the same <em>household</em> when they share a computed {@link Household#id(String,
15	 * String) householdId} (same last name and postcode). A second owner in an existing household is a
16	 * household duplicate and is rejected — <em>unless</em> the request sets {@code sharesHousehold},
17	 * which bypasses this block so the owner is created as a declared household member. The
18	 * {@code householdId} is derived from the fields, not linked at create time, so members of a
19	 * household always share it automatically.
20	 *
21	 * <p>Independently, two owners that are the same contact (matching telephone and email — the
22	 * {@link OwnerIdentity#contactKey(String, String) contactKey}) collide regardless of household;
23	 * {@code sharesHousehold} does not bypass that, since a declared member is a distinct contact.
24	 *
25	 * <p>Runs after {@link RequireOwnerFields} has normalized and published the body and before
26	 * {@link BuildOwner}/{@link SaveOwner} persist the new owner.
27	 */
28	public class RequireUniqueIdentity {
29	
30	    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
31	            throws DuplicateIdentityException {
32	        boolean sharesHousehold = Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold());
33	        String householdId = Household.id(request.getLastName(), request.getPostcode());
34	        String contactKey = OwnerIdentity.contactKey(request.getTelephone(), request.getEmail());
35	        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
36	            String existingKey = OwnerIdentity.contactKey(existing.getTelephone(), existing.getEmail());
37	            if (contactKey.equals(existingKey)) {
38	                throw new DuplicateIdentityException(
39	                        "An owner with the same identity already exists");
40	            }
41	            if (!sharesHousehold
42	                    && householdId.equals(Household.id(existing.getLastName(), existing.getPostcode()))) {
43	                throw new DuplicateIdentityException(
44	                        "An owner in the same household already exists");
45	            }
46	        }
47	    }
48	}
